    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## MongoDB Sharded Cluster Analyzer - v11 AI + data-quality guardrails\n\nBatched architecture remains unchanged.\n\nData-quality fix:\n- seven-day completeness now accounts for maxDataPoints-induced query downsampling\n- effective expected interval is aligned to an integer multiple of the configured interval\n- a small query/extraction error count produces usable_with_caution rather than automatically invalidating the whole report\n- exact query/extraction error details are carried into the report\n\nAI payload reduction:\n- full MongoDB/sharding metric-name arrays removed from Gemini input\n- only capability booleans and metric counts are sent\n\nAI guardrails:\n- no replica-set health claims from state composition alone\n- no balancer failure/inactivity inference from zero moveChunk deltas\n- no qualitative oplog headroom/recovery sufficiency/oplog-size speculation\n- no lag-cause speculation or P99/max mixing\n- no client traffic/load-balancer inference from similar mongos counters\n- no WiredTiger working-set/cache-sizing inference from occupancy\n- no disk-busy cause attribution\n- no invented MongoDB helper commands\n- no speculative filesystem causes\n- exact identifier integrity required",
