x.chunks_last ?? max.chunks_avg)}) and ${min.shard} the smallest (${fmt(min.chunks_last ?? min.chunks_avg)}). Chunk count is not equivalent to data size or shard-key quality.`\n  );\n}\n\nif (shardPrimaryRows.length > 1) {\n  const sortedRead =\n    [...shardPrimaryRows]\n      .filter(x => finite(x.read_avg) !== null)\n      .sort((a,b) => b.read_avg - a.read_avg);\n\n  const sortedWrite =\n    [...shardPrimaryRows]\n      .filter(x => finite(x.write_avg) !== null)\n      .sort((a,b) => b.write_avg - a.write_avg);\n\n  if (sortedRead[0] || sortedWrite[0]) {\n    assessment.push(\n      `**Observed shard workload distribution:** ${sortedRead[0] ? `${sortedRead[0].shard} had the largest observed shard-PRIMARY read-rate share (${fmt(sortedRead[0].read_share_of_observed_shard_primary_rate_pct)}%)` : 'read-rate share unavailable'}; ${sortedWrite[0] ? `${sortedWrite[0].shard} had the largest observed shard-PRIMARY write-rate share (${fmt(sortedWrite[0].write_share_of_observed_shard_primary_rate_pct)}%)` : 'write-rate share unavailable'}. These are observed PRIMARY rates, not exact application-operation shares or proof of a shard-key issue.`\n    );\n  }\n}\n\nconst dataLeader =\n  [...shardDataRows]\n    .filter(x => finite(x.data_size_bytes) !== null)\n    .sort((a,b) => b.data_size_bytes - a.data_size_bytes)[0] || null;\n\nif (dataLeader) {\n  assessment.push(\n    `**Current per-shard dbStats footprint:** ${dataLeader.shard} had the largest PMM-exported dbStats dataSize snapshot at ${fmtBytes(dataLeader.data_size_bytes)} (${fmt(dataLeader.data_size_share_pct)}% of the observed per-shard dataSize total). dbStats raw is database-level per-shard context; it is not a direct sharded-collection balance measurement, filesystem usage, or proof of shard-key quality.`\n  );\n}\n\n// Consolidate independent PMM signals only when the same shard leads\n// all of them. This is characterization, not causal diagnosis.\nconst chunkLeader =\n  shardChunkRows.length\n    ? shardChunkRow